{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>אשר עבדתי אותך כהן — for which I have served you until now.</b> \"To my wives\" and not \"to my children,\" like \"וישם דמי מלחמה בשלום\" (I Kings 2:5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The lemma parses כהן as כ + הן = 'until now'; the parenthetical gloss clarifies the argument that the phrase distributes to two objects."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:24.173754466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}